Z||000000||SeanyD||06-25-2000||06:28 PM||||anyone know where to get a half decent rebuild kit(new gaskets, springs, rings ect...) for a good price on the 2.5( 84)??||||reg||1
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||06-25-2000||08:51 PM||||you may want to check with your local machinests. The "performance" rebuild kit for the v6 from fierostore is like $900, but if I take my engine down to Norpa it's $1400 including boring, honing, balancing, hot tank, valve job, new bearings and everything else, not to mention they tear it apart and put it together. $500 and the only thing you don't get it a new cam (which yes is a major player in proformance) but buying one for them to install wouldn't be too bad. Check arround, you may find prices to be cheaper where you are, lord know these east cost places are expensive for labor.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-26-2000||12:28 AM||||if you are going to reuse an 84 replace the rods. You might want to find an 86 motor. It has a roller cam figured in. gets a little more power. you can get the motor form any thing with the 2.5. They are all the same except for some brackets and pulleys.<P>also, NEVER reuse head bolts in the dukes. Either get new bolts or use studs & nuts.||||reg||1
